@node Overview
@chapter Overview

@samp{agent-extras.el} extends the @samp{agent} package with commands that depend on
my own skills@comma{} and so do not belong in a package other people install:

@itemize
@item
A project audit that runs several audit skills in sequence
(@ref{Project audit, , Project audit}).
@item
The post-push CI closeout (@ref{Post-push CI, , Post-push CI}).
@item
A read-only view of @samp{orchestrate-review} runs
(@ref{Orchestration run view, , Orchestration run view}).
@end itemize

@findex agent-extras-add-menu-entries
Loading the file calls @code{agent-extras-add-menu-entries}@comma{} which adds the three
commands to the Tools column of @code{agent-menu} after ``run skill'': audit project
(@samp{t a})@comma{} post-push CI (@samp{t c}) and orchestration run (@samp{t o}). Calling it again
adds nothing.

@node Project audit
@chapter Project audit

@findex agent-extras-audit-project
@vindex agent-extras-audit-skills
@vindex agent-extras-audit-project-directories
The command @code{agent-extras-audit-project} prompts for a backend and a project
directory@comma{} then runs each skill in @code{agent-extras-audit-skills} with @samp{--accept}
through the backend's non-interactive prompt runner. It commits the changes
after each skill that succeeds@comma{} and shows the results in the
@samp{*Agent audit results*} buffer when the last one finishes. It refuses to start
when the directory has uncommitted changes@comma{} since the automatic commits would
include them.

@code{agent-extras-audit-project-directories} holds the directories offered at the
prompt. A directory typed at the prompt is saved to it.

@node Post-push CI
@chapter Post-push CI

@findex agent-extras-post-push-ci
The command @code{agent-extras-post-push-ci} runs the @samp{post-push-ci} skill through
the selected backend with @samp{--no-push --commit HEAD}. Use it after a push has
already happened and you want an agent to inspect GitHub Actions failures@comma{} fix
the root cause@comma{} and continue the authorized CI closeout loop.

@node Inbox monitor drafts
@chapter Inbox monitor drafts

@findex agent-extras-inbox-drafts-file
Loading @samp{agent-extras} sets @code{agent-review-file-function} to
@code{agent-extras-inbox-drafts-file}@comma{} so @samp{m f} (open review file) in the Monitor
section of @code{agent-menu} opens the inbox monitor's drafts file for the
current session: the file where draft replies to the messages routed to that
session's project wait for review@comma{} with the context needed to decide each one.
The function asks the monitor's @samp{inbox-drafts path --cwd DIR} which project
holds the session's directory@comma{} and returns nil (so @samp{m f} reports that the
session has no review file) when the command is missing or no monitored
project holds the directory. After commenting on the drafts@comma{} @samp{m p} (process
review file) asks the session to carry out the comments.

@vindex agent-extras-review-files-directory
@findex agent-extras-review-file-setup
Any file visited under @code{agent-extras-review-files-directory} (the drafts
directory) turns on @code{redline-mode}@comma{} so the CriticMarkup comments on each draft
can be read and written in place@comma{} however the file was opened.

@node Orchestration run view
@chapter Orchestration run view

@findex agent-extras-run-open
@findex agent-extras-run-mode
The command @code{agent-extras-run-open} opens an @samp{orchestrate-review} run JSON file
in a read-only @code{agent-extras-run-mode} buffer. Select the private run file
created by the skill; the command remembers opened filenames for the current
Emacs session and does not scan temporary directories. Each run has its own
view.

The view shows the recorded stage@comma{} phase@comma{} status@comma{} author and reviewer@comma{} and
the latest stage-level progress with the progress file's age. Pending delivery
reconciliation and a recorded incomplete return appear as attention items.
Old progress does not establish that an actor stopped. A returned implementation
is distinct from a completed run; the helper still owns verification evidence
and completion. This view does not validate the full workflow contract.

Session links recheck the recorded native identity before opening a buffer.
An unavailable or replaced session is labeled unavailable. Legacy version-2
runs remain readable@comma{} but actors without recorded identities cannot be linked.
File links open the run record@comma{} progress file@comma{} run directory@comma{} or repository.
The run format does not record ordinary spec/plan paths or blocker descriptions;
the view says so rather than looking through conversations to infer them.

Visible views refresh every five seconds; @samp{g} refreshes immediately and @samp{q}
quits the window. Killing a view cancels its refresh timer. A read failure
replaces the display with an explicit error@comma{} so stale data cannot appear current.
Only local files are supported. Run reads are limited to 4 MiB@comma{} and progress
reads to the final 16 KiB@. The view never submits prompts@comma{} advances phases@comma{}
reads transcripts@comma{} inspects internal tasks@comma{} or starts workers.

